---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import NightChart from "../../components/NightChart.astro";
import PulseLab from "../../components/PulseLab.astro";
import CameraPulse from "../../components/CameraPulse.astro";
import ActivityChart from "../../components/ActivityChart.astro";
import night from "../../data/featured-night.json";
---
<Base title="Pulse" description="From raw light to heartbeat: an explorable built on months of my own wearable data.">
  <h1>Pulse</h1>
  <p class="lede">A ring or a watch doesn't hear your heart. It shines light into your skin and measures how much comes back. Each heartbeat pushes a little more blood under the sensor, so the returning light dips. Everything else, including breathing, footsteps and a twitch of the hand, also changes that light. Getting a heart rate means pulling one rhythm out of all the others.</p>

  <h2>A night in my signals</h2>
  <p>Pick any of the nights I've recorded and drag across the chart. Each moment you pick feeds the experiment below.</p>
  <NightChart night={night} picker />

  <PulseLab />

  <h2>What to try</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Leave movement at zero. The filter finds the beat easily.</li>
    <li>Slide movement toward running. Footsteps land at two to three steps a second, right inside the heart's frequency range, and the estimate locks onto your stride instead of your heart.</li>
    <li>Turn on motion cancellation. The accelerometer tells the algorithm what movement looks like, and it subtracts that from the light. This is the idea behind motion-tolerant wearables, the problem I worked on at Valencell.</li>
  </ol>

  <ActivityChart />

  <CameraPulse />

  <h2>Methods</h2>
  <p class="small">Activities: Suunto watch recordings synced through Strava, with heart rate, cadence and elevation every 2 seconds (run) or 10 seconds (hike); GPS, place names and clock times removed. Data: Oura ring sleep sessions, heart rate and RMSSD every 5 minutes, movement every 30 seconds; clock times removed. Waveform: two-Gaussian pulse model per beat, beat intervals drawn from the recorded heart rate with spread set by RMSSD, breathing at the recorded rate. Processing: zero-phase Butterworth band-pass, normalized-LMS adaptive noise cancellation with the accelerometer as reference, peak detection with an adaptive threshold, heart rate from the median beat interval. All of it runs in your browser; <a href="https://github.com/jacoppock/jacoppock.dev/blob/main/src/scripts/ppg.ts">read the code</a>.</p>
</Base>

<style>
  .lede { font-size: var(--step-1); line-height: 1.5; }
</style>
